{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 Arial;}}\viewkind4\uc1\pard\f0\fs24\b Behavior Tracker Reference Sheet\b0\par\par Files\par - behavior-scorecard.html = page structure and IDs\par - scorelogic.js = logic and Firebase\par - scorecard.css = design and layout\par - README.md = notes and setup\par\par Main app flow\par 1. Load students\par 2. Render cards in studentsGrid\par 3. Click a behavior button\par 4. Write to Firestore\par 5. Realtime listener updates historyList\par\par Important IDs\par - newStudentName\par - addStudentButton\par - studentsGrid\par - historyList\par - loading\par\par Main functions\par - loadStudents()\par - addStudent()\par - recordBehavior(studentId, behaviorName)\par - renderDashboard()\par - selectStudent(studentId)\par - toggleBehaviors(studentId)\par - setupRealtimeUpdates(filter)\par - filterBehaviors(filterType)\par - deleteStudent(studentId)\par\par Event listener pattern\par Use one delegated listener on the grid instead of many ad hoc listeners.\par\par studentsGrid.addEventListener('click', (event) => {\par    const btn = event.target.closest('.behavior-button');\par    if (btn) {\par        recordBehavior(btn.dataset.studentId, btn.dataset.behaviorName);\par    }\par});\par\par Custom student icons\par Use a stable icon selector based on the student ID:\par\par function getStudentIcon(studentId) {\par    const icons = ['🌞', '🌿', '⭐', '🎨', '🚀', '🌈', '🦋', '🏕️'];\par    let total = 0;\par    for (let i = 0; i < studentId.length; i++) {\par        total += studentId.charCodeAt(i);\par    }\par    return icons[total % icons.length];\par}\par\par Or use real files:\par const icons = ['icons/sun.svg', 'icons/rocket.svg', 'icons/star.svg'];\par\par Then render:\par <img src="${getStudentIcon(student.id)}" alt="student icon">\par\par Debugging order\par 1. node --check scorelogic.js\par 2. browser console\par 3. HTML/JS ID match\par 4. Firestore auth + rules\par 5. single fix, then re-test\par\par Important lesson\par The real issue was not JS being impossible. It was a combination of small syntax mistakes, messy event binding, and Firestore rules blocking access.\par\par If you ever need to fix this again without AI:\par - run the syntax check\par - open the console\par - match IDs exactly\par - inspect Firebase auth and rules\par - fix one root cause at a time\par}